---
/* THE TURN
   This was the page's largest claim stated as a sentence and shown as nothing.
   ADR 0046 is a claim about wiring, so it is drawn as wiring. The two states
   differ in one readable quantity: how many connections the product itself has
   to own. Five, or one. */
import Wiring from '../islands/Wiring.tsx';
---
<section class="turn plane" id="turn">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="turn__lead rise">
      {/* The `{' '}` is load-bearing. Astro collapses the newline between the
          closing tag and the next word to nothing, not to a space, so the
          built page read "their own product.WordScript keeps it". */}
      <span class="dim">Most dictation tools end at the cursor. The ones that keep
      anything keep it inside their own product.</span>{' '}
      WordScript keeps it in a directory <em>your own tools already open</em>.
    </p>

    <Wiring client:visible />
  </div>
</section>
